      "id": 1,
      "text": "Samuel Duncan founded Duncansville in 1830, buying land on the western bank of the creek and plotting the town that bears his name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duncansville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "East of the creek, Jacob Walters laid out a settlement called Walterstown, which later merged with Duncansville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duncansville%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Duncansville Historical Society was founded on August 12, 1980, preserving the borough’s rich heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
